;; App configuration — read once at load. Everything here has a sane default;
;; the file exists so the defaults are visible and overridable, not because
;; anything requires editing.
{;; The base URL printed on public-facing surfaces (the create page's marquee,
 ;; invite links, exports). nil = derive from the request, which honors
 ;; X-Forwarded-Host/Proto and is therefore already correct on Cloud Run.
 ;; Set it only to force a specific address — e.g. a custom domain, or showing
 ;; the production URL while developing locally:
 ;;   :public-base-url "https://swyx-cfp-saas-killer-109637679549.us-west1.run.app"
 :public-base-url nil

 ;; Google Sign-In (server-side OIDC). The client ID is public by design — it
 ;; appears in every redirect URL. The client SECRET lives in secrets.clj land
 ;; (secrets/google-oauth-client.txt locally, Secret Manager on Cloud Run);
 ;; the button only renders when both halves are present.
 :google-client-id "109637679549-j9espgi36hpq3agjffq6crhao9k4logg.apps.googleusercontent.com"

 ;; Demo mode (bd -o42): the login page grows one-click sign-in buttons for the
 ;; seeded demo people (organizer/reviewer/speaker). OFF by default since
 ;; 2026-08-11: dev matches curtaincallcfp (demo-off), and the ghost-map
 ;; replay demo replaced canned personas as the stranger's door. A dedicated
 ;; demo instance can still opt in with DEMO_MODE=true.
 :demo-mode false}
